docs/design/intent.md:4:`notes-lib` is an in-memory notes library (`NoteStore`, `searchNotes`) that can only be used in-process. Other clients need to create, read and search notes over HTTP, and operators need a container they can deploy and smoke-test locally. The API is a thin edge over the existing library. It reuses `NoteStore` and `searchNotes` unchanged and keeps the repository's conventions: kebab-case files, library functions that never throw and return `Result<T>`, tests in `tests/` run by `npm test`, and no new runtime dependencies (`node:http` only).
docs/design/intent.md:11:- `docker compose up` serves the API on host port 8081, and `npm run smoke` exits 0 against it (non-zero on any failed check).
